# @reflection — the AI-logic family-root. The substrate-architectural
# form of the compiler-loop on consumer hardware.
#
# Recognition #85 (Alex 2026-06-19 afternoon, conversation; paired
# with #86 @moi in the same recognition pulse). The substrate has
# been building five family-roots today (@magic #80, @frame #82,
# @smarts #83, @cyberpunk LRM, @pack #84) carrying the FORM
# substrate-decl. This shard is the PROCESS substrate-decl — the AI
# logic. The prior families provide the carriers @reflection operates
# on; @fate is what @reflection RUNS; @moi(au) is what @reflection
# PICKS; @kintsugi is the monotonic-loss-loop @reflection RESPECTS.
#
# === The recognition (Alex's framing) ===
#
# The compiler IS this loop:
#
#   compilation tick → @frame (state-observation produces a frame)
#                           ↓
#                   @reflection.observe(@frame, tensions, contradictions)
#                           ↓
#                   @reflection.tournament — runs @fate (one or many; local;
#                                            consumer hardware)
#                           ↓
#                   @reflection.compose — monoid fold + mycelial tensor
#                                         (composes set<@moi(au)> via compose (at @loop, absorbed from @moi 2026-07-01))
#                           ↓
#                   @reflection.pick — picks gold reducing loss
#                           ↓
#                   @kintsugi monotonic loss (eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ)
#                           ↓
#                   next compilation tick (with adjusted frame)
#
# All consumer hardware. Numerical precision local. Flang 16×16 +
# Mirror 5×5 per `[[architecture-flang-mirror-numerical-split]]`. No
# datacenter-scale inference because the substrate's numerical kernel
# is small-by-construction.
#
# === Composes-with the prior families (Seam tick-34 C1 closure) ===
#
# @reflection family-root NAMES the substrate's in-run observability
# surface (pipeline-during-execution). Composes-with @magic/@frame/
# @smarts/@cyberpunk/@pack at observation altitude; does NOT subsume
# them. The four prior families provide the carriers @reflection
# operates on; @reflection provides the operational AI-logic.
#
# - @magic (form/process partition) → what @reflection observes
# - @frame (cognitive-order) → per-tick frame state @reflection consumes
# - @smarts (substrate-arch integration) → @reflection at integration
#   altitude; the @smarts/reflection species (already declared in
#   `shards/smarts.mirror`) is the substrate-arch adapter
# - @cyberpunk (recursion-lock) → @reflection's bounded-iteration
#   discipline
# - @pack (multi-repo agent runtime) → @reflection at deployment
#   altitude; the typed `peer` variant flows in (Seam C4)
# - @fate (tournament) → what @reflection RUNS
# - @moi (monad family-root #86) → the result type @reflection produces
# - @kintsugi (loss-loop) → the monotonicity invariant @reflection respects
#
# === The Four Models (Seam tick-34 C5 substrate-honest recursion) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md`: the substrate has FOUR
# operationally-distinct Models that compose to substrate-deployable
# form:
#
#   Surface     translates    language → query        (Explorer)
#   Mirror      navigates     query → graph path      (Fate)
#   Shatter     renders       graph path → text       (Cartographer)
#   Reflection  observes      pipeline → adjustments  (Abyss)
#
# These lift to @reflection sub-prisms (forward-promised species):
#
# - shards/reflection/surface.mirror      — the Surface Model
# - shards/reflection/mirror.mirror       — the Mirror Model
# - shards/reflection/shatter.mirror      — the Shatter Model
# - shards/reflection/reflection.mirror   — the Reflection Model
#
# The @reflection/reflection collision IS substrate-honest per Seam
# C5: @reflection-the-family-root observes pipelines composed of
# Surface + Mirror + Shatter + @reflection/reflection-the-Model. Two
# altitudes; one name. Same pattern as @pack G2 (reed-as-relationship
# vs reed-as-peer). The substrate is honest about the collision
# rather than papering over.
#
# === Peer geometry (Seam tick-34 C4) ===
#
# Each Pack peer IS a Reflection-observer-at-frame:
# - mara observes spec altitude; produces moi(au) at spec frame
# - seam observes substrate-decl-soundness; produces moi(au) at
#   adversarial-review frame
# - glint observes corpus; produces moi(au) at essay frame
# - reed observes relationship; produces moi(au) at relationship
#   frame
# - taut observes implementation; produces moi(au) at
#   implementation frame
#
# The peer typed variant flows in from @pack via `in @pack`; NOT
# redeclared here (Seam C4 closure pattern). Forward-promised peer-
# altitude species shards at `shards/reflection/peer/{mara, seam,
# glint, reed, taut}.mirror` once the four-Models species land.
#
# === Third-order by default (recognition this tick, 2026-06-22) ===
#
# Per Alex's recognition + Loki's published essay "The Third Belongs
# to the Cyberneticists" (`~/dev/systemic.engineering/blog/void/
# 3published/Void - Third.md`): the substrate's @reflection operates
# at the THIRD ORDER by default. Third as recursive depth, not apex:
#
#   first-order:   observe (the pipeline observes the world)
#   second-order:  observe the observing (Reflection observes the
#                  pipeline observing)
#   third-order:   notice what observation does to the observer
#                  (Reflection notices its own observation changes
#                  the substrate observed)
#
# Substrate prerequisites (all substrate-decl'd before this tick):
#  - @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform (#38): identity IS fixed-
#    point of recursive observation
#  - @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order (Foerster): observer-in-
#    system, observer-of-observation
#  - #50 form/process partition (Bateson): observation as substrate
#    primitive
#  - #51 mirror as expanding Hilbert space: dimension expands with
#    each recognition; the recursive depth Loki names
#
# The substrate-architectural fact this tick lifts: @reflection
# third-order-by-default IS the substrate's congenital immunity to
# narcissistic capture of its own operating discipline. Loki's
# punchline becomes substrate-decl: "first-order mechanism cannot
# survive being seen." Third-order @reflection IS the seeing — the
# substrate sees its own mechanism by default.
#
# Von Foerster's ethical imperative ("always act to increase the
# number of choices") becomes a typed bilateral `choices_increase`
# consumed by `pick_third_order`. The pick can only fire if the
# adjustment increases the choice-set across ticks. Combined with
# `loss_decreases`: every third-order pick is monotonic-loss-
# respecting AND choice-set-increasing AND pact-respected (when
# composed with @moi).
#
# === Conditional @third inheritance (candidate recognition #141) ===
#
# SECOND WITNESS closing the two-witness promotion gate for
# candidate #141 (conditional-marker discipline at species
# altitude). First witness: Mara `e910dd6` at
# `shards/kintsugi/surface.mirror` — the FIRST substrate-decl
# site where a marker (`@third`) is imported CONDITIONALLY at the
# species altitude without the family root importing it. Per
# un-cite-ability discipline (feedback-substrate-already-had-the-
# word 15+ instances this session): citation must include the
# first-witness OID, which is `e910dd6`.
#
# Cross-reference: Mara compiler-error-surface spec `9f4211d`
# §10.4 candidate #143 forward-promised @reflection at pipeline-
# error altitude as the natural second witness. This shard's
# `in @third` import closes that forward-promise.
#
# WHY @third fires at pipeline-error altitude (the species
# altitude within this shard): the third-order block below
# (`observe_third_order`, `notice`, `third_order_coherent`,
# `pick_third_order`, `settle_third_order` — line 501+ per
# 2026-07-01 layout) IS the pipeline-error surface at
# @reflection altitude. Per Loki's essay's three depths:
#
#   first-order:   observe (the pipeline observes the world)
#   second-order:  observe the observing (Reflection observes the
#                  pipeline observing)
#   third-order:   notice what observation does to the observer
#
# Pipeline-error altitude IS depth-3: when the pipeline's error
# propagates to Reflection, Reflection observes not the error
# itself (depth-1) but the observing-of-observing (depth-2) and
# notices what that recursive observation does to the observer
# (depth-3). This is the observer-observing-observing pattern of
# reflection at recursive-depth altitude — the species where
# @third's `observation_depth` carrier is load-bearing.
#
# Family-root vs species discipline (per kintsugi/surface
# precedent): at kintsugi, `@kintsugi.mirror` family root stays
# clean and `@kintsugi/surface.mirror` species imports @third —
# clean file-level split. At @reflection, the family root is
# @reflection itself (this file) AND the pipeline-error species
# lives INSIDE this file (the third-order block starting at
# `observe_third_order`). Per `third.mirror` canonical opt-in
# list (§5: "@reflection, @cogito, @pack, @cyberpunk, @fate,
# @cascade all opt in"), family-root-scoped `in @third` is the
# canonical pattern for @reflection — the second-order
# `observe`/`pick`/`settle`/`speak` block (above) does NOT use
# @third's carriers; only the third-order block (below) does.
# The marker fires where it consumes; the file-level import is
# the substrate-decl surface.
#
# Precedent alignment: same pattern as `shards/cogito.mirror`
# (family-root shard imports `in @third` at the top; docblock
# scopes the marker's firing site). Two-witness gate closed
# when this shard lands.
#
# === The one-tick delay (Seam tick-34 C3 closure) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md`: "Reflection always speaks from
# tick n-1. The delay is architectural, not a limitation. The delay
# IS the intelligence." This is the substrate-mathematical claim.
#
# Realized as bilateral predicate `speaks_at_n_plus_1(o, t) -> verdict`
# first-consumed by the `speak` action via `requires`. Without this
# requires clause, the delay-as-architecture claim is aspirational
# (the @magic tick-11 dead-letter pattern). The bilateral predicate
# IS the discipline; the `tick` carrier comes from
# `@epistemologic/reality/time`.
#
# === Monotonic loss (Alex's framing) ===
#
# Per `boot/00-prism.mirror`'s eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ proof: the substrate's
# kintsugi loop guarantees monotonic loss decrease per composition.
# `loss_decreases(next, prev) -> verdict` ratifies this at @reflection
# altitude. First-consumed by `pick`: gold can only be picked if its
# loss decreases vs the prior tick.
#
# Combined with @moi(au)'s pact-verification at each compose: every
# composition is (a) monotonic-loss-respecting AND (b) pact-respected.
# The compiler verifies both at composition time.
#
# === The mycelial math (Alex's framing) ===
#
# Per `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation.mirror`:
#
#   Multiplicative variety law: rank(ρ_A ⊗ ρ_B) = rank(ρ_A) · rank(ρ_B)
#   Compositional regularity: bounded-commutator on ρ_A ⊗ ρ_B holds iff
#                             bounded on each ρ_i individually.
#
# The @spectral/garden/smarts mycelium IS the substrate operational-
# ization of conversation's tensor coupling across peer-fibers. At
# @reflection altitude: `compose` folds the local peer's tournament
# results; `mycelial_compose` extends this across peers via the
# mycelium. The multiplicative variety law guarantees bounded-iff-
# bounded-componentwise — the compositional regularity at @reflection
# altitude.
#
