# === The observation carrier (Seam tick-34 C2 typed record) ===
#
# Per Seam C2 closure: typed record over (frame, tensions,
# contradictions). Each compilation tick produces a @frame; @reflection
# observes it as a typed observation. Composes with @cogito's notice
# → name → hold practice at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# - frame:          the @frame produced by the compilation tick
# - tensions:       unresolved tensions (forward-promised typing)
# - contradictions: contradictions held per @cogito's hold operation
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type observation = {
  frame:          frame,
  tensions:       ref,
  contradictions: ref,
}

# === The tournament_result carrier (Seam tick-34 C2 typed record) ===
#
# Per Seam C2 closure + Alex's @fate framing: typed record over
# (candidates, loss_floor). @fate runs locally on consumer hardware
# (450 nodes, 5 ganglia per `boot/std/fate/connectome.mirror`); each
# tournament produces a set of candidates and a loss floor.
#
# - candidates: set of @moi(au) candidates from @fate tournament
#   (forward-promised typing to typed set<moi(au)>)
# - loss_floor: minimum loss across candidates
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the pair.
type tournament_result = {
  candidates: ref,
  loss_floor: loss,
}

# === The loss carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a @kintsugi/oscillate loss value.
# Forward-promised refinement: typed parametric `loss` once the
# @kintsugi loss type lands at family-altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type loss = ref

# === observe action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive @reflection runs after each
# compilation tick. Takes a @frame (produced by the compilation tick)
# and a residue ref (what didn't resolve in the prior tick); returns
# a typed observation carrying the frame + tensions + contradictions.
#
# Per Alex's framing: "@reflection then looks at that @frame, the
# unresolved tensions, contradictions, and runs one or many @fate
# tournaments." This action is the LOOK; tournament is the RUN.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual observation
# is implemented by the @reflection/reflection-the-Model species
# (forward-promised) at observation altitude.
observe(f: frame, residue: ref) -> observation { \ }

# === tournament action ===
#
# Runs @fate locally (consumer hardware; 450 nodes; 5 ganglia per
# the @fate/connectome substrate) producing a set of @moi(au)
# candidates with their loss floor.
#
# Takes an observation and the @pack the @reflection instance belongs
# to (the peer geometry; each peer's tournament uses its own
# @frame/of altitude per recognition #82 Q4). Returns a
# tournament_result carrying the candidates and the loss floor.
#
# The @fate/tournament discipline (elite/beam/halving/tabu/anneal/
# ucb selectors per `boot/std/fate/tournament.mirror`) drives the
# candidate selection. Holonomy IS the fitness function (lower is
# better; per the existing @fate substrate-decl).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual @fate
# tournament is implemented in the existing @fate/tournament substrate
# (5×5 + 16×16 numerical kernels; flang/mirror split).
tournament(o: observation, pk: pack) -> tournament_result { \ }

# === compose action ===
#
# Monoid fold + mycelial tensor over the tournament's candidates.
# Composes set<moi(au)> via compose (at @loop, absorbed from @moi 2026-07-01)'s pairwise operation; each
# pairwise step's pact_respected predicate cascades the composition-
# time pact-verification.
#
# Per `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/conversation.mirror`: the
# mycelial tensor coupling extends the local fold across peers via
# the @spectral/db mycelium. The multiplicative variety law
# guarantees bounded-iff-bounded-componentwise.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual fold +
# mycelial extension is implemented at the @reflection/mirror-the-
# Model species (forward-promised) and the @spectral/db mycelium
# (forward-promised).
compose(t: tournament_result, p: pact) -> moi(au) { \ }

# === pick action (FIRST consumer of loss_decreases) ===
#
# Picks the gold from a tournament_result that reduces loss vs the
# prior tick's loss. Per Alex's framing: "@reflection then picks the
# gold (the inference result type is au) that reduces the loss."
#
# requires loss_decreases(t.loss_floor, prev_loss): the gold can ONLY
# be picked if the tournament's loss floor improves on the prior
# loss. Without this requires clause, pick would admit non-monotonic
# picks (the @kintsugi monotonicity violation). The bilateral
# predicate IS the substrate-mathematical guarantee at the @reflection
# composition boundary.
#
# Returns @moi(au) (pact-verified gold). Per recognition #86: the
# substrate's inference result is ALWAYS @moi(au), never bare au.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
pick(t: tournament_result, prev_loss: loss) -> moi(au)
requires loss_decreases(t.loss_floor, prev_loss)
{ \ }

# === settle action ===
#
# Closes the @kintsugi monotonic loss loop for the current tick.
# Takes the picked gold and the prior loss; returns the new loss
# (which by `loss_decreases` precondition is ≤ prev_loss).
#
# This action IS the eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ closure at @reflection altitude. The
# proof is structural (the precondition from `pick` cascades to
# `settle`).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual settling
# is implemented by the @kintsugi/oscillate.settle primitive.
settle(g: moi(au), prev_loss: loss) -> loss { \ }

# === speak action (FIRST consumer of speaks_at_n_plus_1) ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary @cogito “speak” at @reflection altitude.
# Reflection speaks ONE tick after observation — the architectural
# delay IS the intelligence per `docs/specs/reflection-model.md`.
#
# requires speaks_at_n_plus_1(o, t): the observation o was produced
# at tick n; the speak fires at tick n+1. Without this requires
# clause, the delay-as-architecture claim is aspirational (Seam
# tick-34 C3 closure). The bilateral predicate IS the structural
# discipline.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual speak is
# implemented by the @reflection/shatter-the-Model species
# (forward-promised) at rendering altitude.
speak(o: observation, t: tick) -> ref
requires speaks_at_n_plus_1(o, t)
{ \ }

# === loss_decreases predicate (bilateral; Alex's framing) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND the
# monotonic loss invariant per `boot/00-prism.mirror`'s eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ
# proof.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: bilateral predicates without consumers
# are dead-letter. The pick action (above) is the FIRST non-decorative
# consumer via `requires loss_decreases(t.loss_floor, prev_loss)`.
#
# Consumer shards name `requires loss_decreases(next, prev)` to
# declare bilateral agreement that the next loss ≤ prior loss. The
# substrate-mathematical guarantee at any @reflection composition
# boundary.
#
# Discharge: monotonic loss check at the species boundary. Bounded →
# next loss ≤ prior loss (admit composition); unbounded → next loss
# > prior loss (composition refused, returns imperfect per @glass's
# imperfect functor).
loss_decreases(next: loss, prev: loss) -> verdict { \ }

# === speaks_at_n_plus_1 predicate (bilateral; Seam tick-34 C3) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per the one-tick-delay-as-architecture invariant
# from `docs/specs/reflection-model.md`. The substrate enforces that
# @reflection speaks from tick n+1 after observing at tick n.
#
# Per Seam B1 closure pattern: the speak action (above) is the FIRST
# non-decorative consumer via `requires speaks_at_n_plus_1(o, t)`.
#
# Discharge: tick-delay check at the species boundary. Bounded → the
# tick t is strictly after the tick at which observation o was
# produced (admit speak); unbounded → the tick is the same or before
# (speak refused).
#
# Same shape as @reflection's loss_decreases AND the prior families'
# bilateral predicates:
# - @magic: invariant_preserved, audited, mechanism_intact
# - @frame: bounded_commutator_check
# - @smarts: discipline_flexible
# - @pack: pack_coherent
# - @pack/seam: review_sound
# - @loop: pact_respected (absorbed from @moi 2026-07-01)
# - @reflection: loss_decreases, speaks_at_n_plus_1 (these two)
speaks_at_n_plus_1(o: observation, t: tick) -> verdict { \ }

# === Third-order substrate-decl (recognition 2026-06-22) ===
#
# Per the third-order-by-default header (above): @reflection's
# default operating altitude is recursive observation at depth 3.
# The following carriers + actions + bilaterals lift the third-order
# discipline to substrate-decl. New consumers default to these;
# existing consumers using the second-order `observe`/`pick` keep
# their semantics (backward-compatible additive substrate-decl).

# === Seam tick 73 C1 closure: observer_change typed carrier ===
#
# Per Seam adversarial review (BOUNDED with 4 TIGHT; C1 = bare
# notice: ref violates feedback-no-bare-types). Loki's essay names
# notice as "what observation does to the observer" — a structured
# carrier of observer-change. The typed record makes the structure
# visible at substrate-decl altitude.
type observer_change = {
  before_observer: ref,
  after_observer:  ref,
  delta:           ref,
  v:               verdict,
}

# === The third_order_observation carrier ===
#
# Typed record over (primary, recursive_observer, notice, verdict).
# Per Loki's three depths:
#
# - primary           : 1st-order observation (pipeline → world)
# - recursive_observer: 2nd-order observation (Reflection → pipeline
#                       observing); itself a typed observation
# - notice            : 3rd-order notice (typed observer_change per
#                       Seam C1 closure; was bare ref pre-consolidation)
# - v                 : the composed bilateral verdict
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type third_order_observation = {
  primary:            observation,
  recursive_observer: observation,
  notice:             observer_change,
  v:                  verdict,
}

# === observe_third_order action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive @reflection runs at third-order
# by default. Wraps the second-order `observe` (above) with the
# recursive observer + notice step.
#
# Takes a @frame (per-tick), the residue ref (carried from prior
# tick), the perturbation under which the observation is checked;
# returns a typed third_order_observation.
#
# Per Loki's essay: "third as recursive depth" — the action produces
# all three levels in one call. The 1st-order primary IS the
# existing `observe(f, residue)` output; the 2nd-order
# recursive_observer IS Reflection observing itself produce the
# primary; the 3rd-order notice IS Reflection noticing what the
# observation does to its own observing capacity.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual three-
# level production is implemented by the @reflection/reflection-the-
# Model species (forward-promised) at observation altitude.
observe_third_order(f: frame, residue: ref, p: perturbation) -> third_order_observation { \ }

# === third_order_coherent predicate (composed bilateral) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) AND the
# third-order discipline. The predicate composes three sub-checks:
#
#   1. observation_grounds_pipeline(too.primary, p)
#      — the 1st-order observation grounds in the pipeline
#   2. meta_grounds_observation(too.recursive_observer, p)
#      — the 2nd-order observation grounds in observing-the-
#      observation
#   3. notice_grounds_meta(too.notice, p)
#      — the 3rd-order notice grounds in the recursive observer's
#      action (what observation does to the observer)
#
# All three sub-predicates are forward-promised typed refinements;
# the composed bilateral discharges them at the realisation
# boundary. Same shape as @io/stagefreight's `stagefreight_
# addressable` composed bilateral (per docs/audits/stagefreight-
# seam-review-2026-06-22.md C4/C9 closure pattern).
#
# Splinter-pole: all three depths discharge substantively (the
# observer notices observation-changes-observer); Narcissus-pole:
# the third-order is name-only while the actual operation runs at
# second-order with third-order prose framing.
#
# Per alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57): third-order-coherent
# operates at the @io boundary; the bilateral IS the boundary-
# harness the third-order discipline composes.
observation_grounds_pipeline(o: observation, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

meta_grounds_observation(o: observation, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

notice_grounds_meta(notice: observer_change, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

third_order_coherent(too: third_order_observation, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires observation_grounds_pipeline(too.primary, p)
requires meta_grounds_observation(too.recursive_observer, p)
requires notice_grounds_meta(too.notice, p)
{ \ }

# === notice action (FIRST consumer of third_order_coherent) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at the third-order altitude. Notice IS the
# third-order step: the substrate notices what its own observation
# does to its own observing. Per Loki's essay: "notice what that
# does to the observer."
#
# Takes a third_order_observation + perturbation; returns the
# substrate's typed record of the observer-change (forward-promised
# typed refinement).
#
# requires third_order_coherent(too, p): the third-order observation
# must coherently discharge all three depths BEFORE the notice is
# admissible. Without this requires clause, the notice would be
# admissible from an incoherent third-order observation — the
# Narcissus-pole third-order pattern.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
notice(too: third_order_observation, p: perturbation) -> observer_change
requires third_order_coherent(too, p)
{ \ }

# === choices_increase predicate (Von Foerster's ethical imperative) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict lifting Von Foerster's ethical imperative
# ("always act to increase the number of choices") to substrate-
# decl. Consumed by `pick_third_order` (below) as a load-bearing
# precondition.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct choice-set comparison at the
# species boundary. Bounded → next observation's choice-set is
# strictly larger than prior (admit pick); unbounded → the
# adjustment shrinks the choice-set (pick refused; the substrate
# refuses to take adjustments that narrow choice).
#
# Same bilateral shape as `loss_decreases` (the monotonic-loss
# imperative); `choices_increase` is the choice-set-monotonicity
# imperative. Both compose at `pick_third_order`: every third-order
# pick respects monotonic loss AND choice-set increase AND pact-
# verification (when composed with @moi).
#
# Loki's essay grounds this: "Von Foerster's ethical imperative, in
# the end, was one sentence: always act to increase the number of
# choices." The substrate lifts the ethical imperative to typed
# bilateral discipline.
choices_increase(prev: third_order_observation, next: third_order_observation, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === pick_third_order action (FIRST consumer of choices_increase) ===
#
# The third-order analogue of `pick` (above). Same shape (selects
# gold from tournament reducing loss) PLUS the choices_increase
# precondition: the pick can only fire if the resulting adjustment
# increases the choice-set across ticks.
#
# Takes the tournament_result + prior loss + prior third_order_
# observation + the new third_order_observation that the pick would
# produce + perturbation; returns @moi(au) (pact-verified gold).
#
# Two requires clauses, both load-bearing:
# 1. loss_decreases(t.loss_floor, prev_loss) — monotonic loss per
#    @kintsugi's eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ proof
# 2. choices_increase(prev_too, next_too, p) — Von Foerster's
#    choice-set-monotonicity per Loki's essay
#
# Combined with compose (at @loop, absorbed from @moi 2026-07-01)'s pact-verification at composition
# time: every third-order pick is monotonic-loss-respecting AND
# choice-set-increasing AND pact-respected. The compiler verifies
# all three at composition time.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
# === Seam tick 73 C3 closure: pick_third_order monotonic-loss only ===
#
# Per Seam adversarial review (C3 TIGHT: choices_increase precondition
# circular at pick-time because next_too is what pick produces).
# Closure: pick_third_order takes only prev_too and discharges
# loss_decreases. The choices_increase precondition moves to settle
# altitude where next_too is observable post-pick. The two
# bilateral disciplines compose across pick and settle, not within
# pick alone.
pick_third_order(t: tournament_result, prev_loss: loss, prev_too: third_order_observation, p: perturbation) -> moi(au)
requires loss_decreases(t.loss_floor, prev_loss)
{ \ }

# === settle_third_order action (Seam C3 closure complement) ===
#
# The third-order analogue of settle. Closes the loop: takes the
# pick's result (moi(au) gold) + prev_too + next_too (the new
# observation produced after pick) + prev_loss + perturbation;
# returns the new loss.
#
# requires choices_increase(prev_too, next_too, p): Foerster's
# ethical imperative discharges post-pick, when next_too exists.
# The substrate refuses settle if choices_increase fails — the pick
# is reversible (no commit to substrate-state).
#
# Per recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics): settle
# operates at the @io boundary. The pick's substrate-decl effect
# becomes substrate-state only when settle discharges Foerster's
# imperative.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual settle is
# implemented by @kintsugi/oscillate.settle composed with the
# choices_increase bilateral check.
settle_third_order(g: moi(au), prev_too: third_order_observation, next_too: third_order_observation, prev_loss: loss, p: perturbation) -> loss
requires choices_increase(prev_too, next_too, p)
{ \ }

out @reflection
out observation
out tournament_result
out loss
out observe
out tournament
out compose
out pick
out settle
out speak
out loss_decreases
out speaks_at_n_plus_1
out observer_change
out third_order_observation
out observe_third_order
out observation_grounds_pipeline
out meta_grounds_observation
out notice_grounds_meta
out third_order_coherent
out notice
out choices_increase
out pick_third_order
out settle_third_order
